{
  "answer": "**Trace of `console.print(\"Hello [bold]world[/bold]\")`**\n\n1. **Entry:** `Console.print` (`rich/console.py:1646`) gets `objects = (\"Hello [bold]world[/bold]\",)`. Soft-wrap and crop settings are resolved at 1689\u20131696.\n\n2. **Buffer scope:** `with self:` (1698) calls `__enter__` \u2192 `_enter_buffer()`, which increments `_buffer_index` (851\u2013854, 807\u2013809). Output is held in `self._buffer` until the outermost scope exits.\n\n3. **Collect renderables:** `_collect_renderables` (1699, defined at 1494) sees a `str` and calls `render_str` (1554).\n\n4. **Markup parsing:** `render_str` (1403) calls `render_markup` when markup is enabled (1435\u20131436). In `rich/markup.py:106`, `render` returns a plain `Text` if there's no `[` (128\u2013132). Otherwise it walks `_parse(markup)` (153), appending plain text and pushing a style span for `[bold]`, which is closed by `[/bold]` (159\u2013160). The result is a `Text` with a bold span over \"world\".\n\n5. **Render to segments:** `Console.render` (1311\u20131318) calls `Text.__rich_console__`, which calls `Text.render` (`rich/text.py:707`). That yields `Segment`s for each styled run, with styles resolved via `console.get_style` (724\u2013727). Back in `print`, `render` is called per renderable (1722\u20131725). The output is then `split_and_crop_lines`-ed to console width (1743\u20131748) and extended into `self._buffer`.\n\n6. **Flush:** On leaving `with self:`, `__exit__` \u2192 `_exit_buffer` (811\u2013814) decrements the index and calls `_check_buffer` (2038). That calls `_write_buffer` (2053). Since `_buffer_index == 0`, it renders the buffer to a string with `_render_buffer` (2088 or 2116; 2126\u20132148). This emits ANSI codes via `style.render` (2138) and strips color if `no_color` is set (2133\u20132134).\n\n7. **Write:** The string goes to `self.file.write` (2097 on modern Windows, with 32 KB batching at 2094\u20132111; 2118 elsewhere). Then `self.file.flush()` (2123) and the buffer is cleared (2124).\n\n**Not verified:** I did not read `Style.render` or the `_parse` tokenizer internals, so the exact ANSI escape generation and tag-matching details are unchecked.",
